  <!--Compared to the flagship product of Stahl Arms, the STA-52 V2 is alot like any other remake, lower quality and cheaply made. Still a fine gun in its own right, its only used in times of desperation or great national threat.-->
  
  <ThingDef ParentName="HelghastBaseHumanMakeableGun">
    <defName>Gun_HG_StA52gII</defName>
    <label>StA-52 V2 Rifle</label>
    <description>Stahl Arms' signature weapon, arguably their single greatest product in terms of sales targets and mass appeal, the StA-52 v2 is often mistaken for the V1 rifle, with casual observers forgetting is more complicated design used in the Helghan shock armies. This is because while the 'v1' did receive large scale deployment in those divisions, the rest of the Helghan military was standardized on the v2. In truth the v2 variant of the rifle is not actually an improvement on the design in any meaningful way, but a considerable downgrade- so for propaganda reasons both guns are referred to by the same name- the 'v1 and v2' designations are limited only to internal corporate documentation and ISA armory manifests. Regardless, the same caseless ammunition is used, the weapon length is noticeably shorter, which cut down on weight and costs compared to its predeccessor. The underslung shotgun and integrated optic were removed in favor of rails and a built in flashlight, which typically were not used. This weapon was designed by Committee to meet late war production targets. By the wars end, enough StA-52's were produced to arm every single Helghan man, woman, and child.</description>
	<techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
